{"name":"Walking Stick","hex":"#a2785d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"walking stick","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tool, such as a cane, used to ease pressure on the legs, and to aid stability, when walking.","A stick insect (order Phasmida)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/walking_stick"}],"entries":[{"title":"Walking stick","blocks":[{"text":"A walking stick is a device used primarily to aid walking, provide postural stability or support, or assist in maintaining a good posture. Some designs also serve as a fashion accessory, or are used for self-defense."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Une_canne_de_marchand_Ch%C3%A2lus.jpg/330px-Une_canne_de_marchand_Ch%C3%A2lus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walking_stick","wikidata":"Q1347864"},{"title":"Walking","blocks":[{"text":"Walking is one of the main gaits of terrestrial locomotion among legged animals. Walking is typically slower than running and other gaits. Walking is defined as an \"inverted pendulum\" gait in which the body vaults over the stiff limb or limbs with each step. This applies regardless of the usable number of limbs—even arthropods, with six, eight, or more limbs, walk. In humans, limited research indicates that walking may be associated with reduced risk of diseases and premature death."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Women_walking_in_Hyderabad_street.jpg/330px-Women_walking_in_Hyderabad_street.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walking","wikidata":"Q6537379"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Walking_stick_with_gilded_knob_Walking_Stick%2C_late_19th_century_%28CH_18418409%29.jpg/500px-Walking_stick_with_gilded_knob_Walking_Stick%2C_late_19th_century_%28CH_18418409%29.jpg?